// Title: Execution of Powershell Script in Public Folder
// Sigma ID: fb9d3ff7-7348-46ab-af8c-b55f5fbf39b4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Max Altgelt (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-06 | Modified: 2022-07-14
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001
// Description: This rule detects execution of PowerShell scripts located in the "C:\Users\Public" folder
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.mandiant.com/resources/evolution-of-fin7
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_public_folder.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-f C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-f \"C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-f %Public%" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fi C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fi \"C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fi %Public%" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fil C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fil \"C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-fil %Public%" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-file C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-file \"C:\\Users\\Public" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-file %Public%")
